github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-10-19T02:00:39Z","label":{"name":"kind/bug","color":"c2e0c6"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1291035469","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/14540#issuecomment-1291035469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/14540","id":1291035469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBlCVUc5M86NN","user":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-10-25T19:27:44Z","updated_at":"2022-10-25T19:28:08Z","body":"This looks like a test issue.\r\n\r\n```\r\n    ddl_func();\r\n\r\n    ASSERT_OK(conn->Execute(\"BEGIN\"));\r\n    // This will fail due to schema version mismatch.\r\n    ASSERT_NOK(executeInsert(conn));\r\n    ASSERT_OK(conn->Execute(\"ROLLBACK\"));\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe expect the Insert (issued from TS1) to fail above because of schema version mismatch. This is because `ddl_func` above starts up a (failing) DDL from some other node (TS2). This only causes the DocDB schema version to increase, however it does not increase the catalog version. Thus the cache in TS1 becomes stale, and requests originating from it fail with SchemaVersionMismatch.\r\n\r\nThis is usually true. However the above is the 4th test in the following function:\r\n```\r\nTEST_F(PgCacheRefreshTest, YB_DISABLE_TEST_IN_TSAN(NewConnectionTransparentRetryTxn)) {\r\n  auto stmt_conn = ASSERT_RESULT(Connect());\r\n  TestSetup(&stmt_conn);\r\n\r\n  // Note that this test looks the same as the previous test, but differs in the fact that every\r\n  // DML operation takes place on a new connection.\r\n  // Test DML transaction interleaved with a DDL operation running on a new connection to the\r\n  // same TServer.\r\n  testTxnConcurrentWithDDL([this] {\r\n    testConcurrentDDL(\"col1\");\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // Test DML transaction interleaved with a DDL operation running on a new connection to a\r\n  // different TServer.\r\n  testTxnConcurrentWithDDL([this] {\r\n    testConcurrentDDLFromDifferentNode(\"col2\");\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // Test DML transaction interleaved with an operation that only causes schema version mismatch\r\n  // through a connection to the same TServer. Here the alter operation causes table cache\r\n  // invalidation on the TServer, therefore no retry is needed.\r\n  testSuccessfulTxnSchemaVersionMismatch([this] {\r\n    testConcurrentSchemaVersionIncrement(\"col3\");\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  FAILING TEST!!\r\n  // Test DML transaction interleaved with an operation that only causes schema version mismatch\r\n  // through a connection to a different TServer.\r\n  auto conn = ASSERT_RESULT(Connect());\r\n  testTxnRetryAfterSchemaVersionMismatch(&conn, [this] {\r\n    testConcurrentSchemaVersionIncrementFromDifferentNode(\"col4\");\r\n  });\r\n``` \r\n\r\nWhen the test fails, I notice this log:\r\n```\r\n[ts-3] I1025 19:20:23.642598 24486 tablet_server.cc:646] Invalidating PgTableCache cache since catalog version incremented\r\n[ts-2] I1025 19:20:23.643218 24412 tablet_server.cc:646] Invalidating PgTableCache cache since catalog version incremented\r\n[ts-1] I1025 19:20:23.643929 24337 tablet_server.cc:646] Invalidating PgTableCache cache since catalog version incremented\r\n[m-1] I1025 19:20:23.746932 24298 catalog_manager.cc:6115] T {sys_catalog_tablet_id} P {m1_peer_id}: Servicing AlterTable request from 127.94.190.1:37569: table { table_id: \"000033e8000030008000000000004000\" } alter_schema_steps { type: ADD_COLUMN add_column { schema { name: \"col4\" type { main: STRING } is_nullable: true is_static: false is_counter: false sorting_type: 0 order: 4 pg_type_oid: 25 } } } transaction { transaction_id: \"\\233\\325Z\\210\\352\\340A3\\261\\022\\204`\\023l\\360\\245\" isolation: SNAPSHOT_ISOLATION status_tablet: \"{transactions_tablet_id2}\" priority: 11766745022811068865 start_hybrid_time: 6826908154483802112 locality: GLOBAL }\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe invalidate the entire cache after a catalog version increment. However the test incorrectly assumes that this will happen immediately after the DDL (Test2). But note above that this happens only after the first heartbeat, that happens at the end of Test3. This means all the caches are wiped just before Test4 starts, therefore TS1 does not have a stale cache when Test4 runs. Therefore we do not hit a schema version mismatch as expected.\r\n\r\nIn the passing run, we can see that the invalidation happens at the end of test2, just before test3:\r\n```\r\n[ts-3] I1025 09:56:00.273761 56311808 tablet_server.cc:646] Invalidating the entire cache since catalog version incremented\r\n[ts-2] I1025 09:56:00.273731 116715520 tablet_server.cc:646] Invalidating the entire cache since catalog version incremented\r\n[ts-1] I1025 09:56:00.273948 181805056 tablet_server.cc:646] Invalidating the entire cache since catalog version incremented\r\n[m-1] I1025 09:56:03.954409 152530944 catalog_manager.cc:6178] T 00000000000000000000000000000000 P 131a8753148041bcbb7568aee9f95243: Servicing AlterTable request from 127.0.0.1:59416: table { table_id: \"000033e8000030008000000000004000\" } alter_schema_steps { type: ADD_COLUMN add_column { schema { name: \"col3\" type { main: STRING } is_nullable: true is_static: false is_counter: false sorting_type: 0 order: 4 pg_type_oid: 25 } } } transaction { transaction_id: \"\\374q\\332v\\t\\225Jz\\210\\017\\240\\017\\361\\356\\255.\" isolation: SNAPSHOT_ISOLATION status_tablet: \"293469b1bd4844a0952dd2802f2a92ae\" priority: 15480939143038399706 start_hybrid_time: 6826872679846604800 locality: GLOBAL }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThus the fix is to wait for heartbeat to complete after Test2. I was able to repro this issue consistently with a release build on my dev-server. To verify this theory I added a simple sleep at the end of test2 and the issue no longer occurs. The fix is to add a wait for heartbeat at the end of test2","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1291035469/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":